# Knowledge Graph Documentation Structure

## Entry Points
- Every documentation directory must have an index.md file
- The docs root directory must have an index.md that links to all subdirectories
- All entry points should clearly describe the contents of their section

## Document Connections
- Use relative links to connect documents within the knowledge graph
- All significant documents must include a "Related Documentation" section
- Ensure bidirectional connections between related documents
- Cross-reference documents across different sections when appropriate

## Document Structure
- Each document should have a clear purpose and scope
- Use headings to organize content hierarchically
- Include introductory paragraphs explaining the document's purpose
- End with a conclusion or summary where appropriate
- Link to supporting documents for additional details

## Maintenance
- Update links when moving or renaming documents
- Remove references to deleted documents
- Maintain consistent terminology across all documents
- Regularly review the documentation structure for completeness and coherence
